            "public_requirement": "Two transistor-level input TIA branches with DC-overload cancellation must accept inp and inn and preserve the specified input bias and overload behavior.",
            "electrical_reason": "Each input drives the emitter of a common-base HBT TIA device whose collector feeds pkdinp/pkdinn and the RF chain. For each branch, the MOS differential sensing pair compares the input against vref and develops gdc_p/gdc_n, which drives Xmn_in_p/Xmn_in_n shunt-current devices; the 350 pF capacitors establish a slow control path without shorting the RF collector path. The symmetric topology is corroborated by the matched nominal and overload input voltages and small measured overload mismatch."
