            "public_requirement": "Two transistor-level gain-controlled RF stages must provide monotonic gain control and the specified transimpedance, bandwidth, and group delay.",
            "electrical_reason": "The signal is AC-coupled from the TIA emitter followers into two successive differential common-emitter HBT stages. In each stage, a fixed NMOS tail path is paralleled by an NMOS path gated by gc, so gc physically changes stage tail current and transconductance rather than merely changing a named measurement node. The measured monotonic 1.706 dB gain span and finite wideband transimpedance support that both stages are connected and responsive; the residual target errors are sizing/performance deviations, not a missing stage."
          }
