            "public_requirement": "A transistor-level peak detector must accept pkdinp and pkdinn and produce a strictly increasing differential detector response at detp and detn.",
            "electrical_reason": "Although active HBT rectifier branches are present, detp receives the low- and high-degeneration devices driven from the P input while detn receives the exactly corresponding devices driven from the N input. Under the required equal-amplitude opposite-polarity differential drive, this bilateral arrangement produces equal time-averaged collector currents on detp and detn rather than a steered differential detected quantity. There is no cross-coupled or differential combining path that converts input amplitude to detp-minus-detn. The effectively zero endpoint differential outputs and failed monotonicity directly reflect this structural output arrangement, not merely detector sizing."
          }
        ]
