            "public_requirement": "A transistor-level AGC amplifier and manual or automatic gain selector must produce agc and select mgc or agc onto gc according to mc.",
            "electrical_reason": "The selector itself is a valid complementary transmission-gate arrangement: mc/mc_b enable the mgc devices in manual mode and the agc devices in automatic mode, consistent with the selector measurements. However, the claimed AGC amplifier Xagp/Xagn has inputs oa and ag_ref only; neither detp nor detn, nor any DC path derived from them, connects to its input network. Consequently agc is not an amplified detector-error control voltage, explaining the measured zero AGC gain. A functioning forced-agc selector cannot substitute for the absent detector-responsive AGC amplifier."
          }
