            "public_requirement": "The required TIA, two RF stages, output buffer, detector, AGC, and selector must form a complete receiver whose finalp and finaln outputs meet the nominal, overload, power, and PAM4 requirements.",
            "electrical_reason": "A forward high-frequency signal chain exists from the input HBT collectors through emitter followers, both VGA stages, and the active output buffer. Nevertheless the required control functions are not coherently integrated: the detector has no valid differential amplitude output and the AGC input network is entirely disconnected from detp/detn. Therefore automatic gc cannot be detector-responsive. In addition, finalp/finaln are attached to the actual buffer outputs only through 1 Mohm series alias resistors, rather than a load-capable RF output connection; they can reproduce an unloaded voltage measurement but do not constitute a credible driven final-output interface. These are material integration defects despite the partial PAM4 measurement."
          }
        ]
      }
